  "contracts": [
    "Keep every original assertion in the whole-comma, target-internalized action and post/pre/compositor sections: 33 positive and three negative assertions, with no polarity change.",
    "The ordinary represented identity graph is a section over TotalOp_cat(A). Its two observations use that existing declared base.",
    "The three arbitrary eta inputs use the actual relative-root-to-identity-root modification direction. General lax FF and arbitrary modifications are retained.",
    "Generic and identity-specialized fixed-target observations use hom_con_int_view and the declared native root. The native arbitrary epsilon remains conventional-lax.",
    "Only the two direct Op_transf comparisons restrict their input to the already-declared StrictTransfor classifier and use its ordinary inclusion on both sides. This explicitly corrects the old invalid general-transpose contract; it is not claimed as the original general comparison.",
    "Strict displayed-view observations use the actual Cat_cart coefficient. The old pre/right stable-head runtime nonconversion remains a normalization boundary, not evidence of non-strict pre/right semantics.",
    "The existing whole conventional pre/right comparison already reduces to an identity. Its capped fdapp1_int_cell previously retained a separate head, so the original positive projection assertion failed.",
    "Three constructor-specific runtime rules join that intrinsic-cell projection and the whole/capped fapp1_con_at_transf identity specialization. They retain the actual transport composite, epsilon, functor parameters, base arrow and filler.",
    "No primitive, unifier, new supplied comparison, operational equality-proof argument or new family/FF restriction is introduced. The general post/left negative and arbitrary-modification observations remain.",
    "The core comment now documents the actual native hom_con_int_view signature and the restricted direct-transpose comparison."
